        "text": "A key lesson from the pandemic is that critical goods necessary for sustaining daily life cannot be fully outsourced.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Fair and equitable international trade is necessary while avoiding excessive outsourcing of vital goods.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "No American policymaker in Washington DC fails to recognize the importance of maintaining domestic production for essential items.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
