    "turn_text": "Yeah, it's more than that pastor. It's 40%. Our labor participation rate right now is only about 60%. That means four out of 10 people are sitting at home not working. They're writing in the wagon. Instead of helping to push or pull the wagon, you and I both know our system here in America, self-governance, government of for and by the people demands that everybody does something to help move us along. That means you either help push the wagon or you help pull the wagon. You don't ride in the wagon unless you have to. We've got 10,000 Americans retiring every single day at age 65 going on Medicare and Social Security roles. We don't have a birth rate to replace that aging retiring workforce. We need every able-bodied American that can work to get back to work. Let's all pull together. We are the greatest nation on the planet. We're the ones that brought virtually every modern convenience known to mankind to the world. And we gave it away benevolently to many other countries. Our technology and our desire for freedom and our stand on our treasured values. has raised more people out of poverty around the world than any other country on the planet. So I think America's got a good idea. We are, as you know, an idea. And it's up to every generation to sustain it. And that starts with everybody doing something to pull or push the wagon. We need Americans to get back to work.",
